# Line endings, pinned rather than left to whatever each machine prefers.
#
# This repo gets cloned onto both Windows and Linux. A shell script checked out
# with CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", which is a
# baffling error for something that looks fine in an editor. So the scripts are
# LF everywhere, and the Windows batch file is CRLF everywhere.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
